<title>DENMARK: Danish Nykredit full year 1996 profits rise.</title>
<headline>Danish Nykredit full year 1996 profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>12-months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>				   (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net result			    2,177 vs 1,964</p>
<p> Losses and bad debt provisions	    312 vs   459</p>
<p> Net interest and fees income	    4,035 vs 3,720</p>
<p> Securities and forex results		714 vs   842</p>
<p> Group pre-tax result			3,158 vs 3,011</p>
<p> Balance		  end-1996 412.3 billion vs 400.5 billion</p>
<p>								 end-1995</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Denmark's biggest mortgage credit firm is Nykredit A/S.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that it expected a pre-tax and securities/forex result for 1997 approaching two billion crowns, compared to 1996's 2.445 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom, 45-33-969652</p>
</text>
